{"id":51,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield","Crystal"],"text":"These Diglett triplets dig over 60 miles below sea level. No one knows what it’s like underground."},{"games":["Sword","LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"A team of Diglett triplets. It triggers huge earthquakes by burrowing 60 miles underground."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!"],"text":"A team of triplets that can burrow to a depth of 60 miles. It’s reported that this triggers an earthquake."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"Dugtrio’s heads are sleek and smooth and incredibly hard. It can dig through any soil with its headbutts."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"While the three of them normally get along splendidly, on rare occasions a huge fight will break out over which head gets to eat first."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"Despite the closeness between this Pokémon and farmers and other people, no one has ever seen the parts of it concealed underground."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"This set of triplets moves cooperatively. It’s the power of teamwork that enables this Pokémon to dig to a depth of 60 miles."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Omega Ruby","Sapphire","Ruby"],"text":"Dugtrio are actually triplets that emerged from one body. As a result, each triplet thinks exactly like the other two triplets. They work cooperatively to burrow endlessly."},{"games":["Y","SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"Extremely powerful, they can dig through even the hardest ground to a depth of over 60 miles."},{"games":["X","FireRed"],"text":"In battle, it digs through the ground and strikes the unsuspecting foe from an unexpected direction."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"Its three heads move alternately, driving it through tough soil to depths of over 60 miles."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"Its three heads bob separately up and down to loosen the soil nearby, making it easier for it to burrow."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"Because the triplets originally split from one body, they think exactly alike. They work cooperatively to burrow endlessly through the ground."},{"games":["Yellow"],"text":"A team of triplets that can burrow over 60 MPH. Due to this, some people think it's an earthquake."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Sand Veil","hidden":false,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's evasiveness in a sandstorm."},{"name":"Arena Trap","hidden":false,"description":"Prevents opposing Pokémon from fleeing from battle."},{"name":"Sand Force","hidden":true,"description":"Boosts the power of Rock-, Ground-, and Steel-type moves in a sandstorm."}],"eggGroups":["Field"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium","habitat":"cave","color":"Brown","shape":"Heads","evolution":{"id":50,"name":"Diglett","condition":null,"children":[{"id":51,"name":"Dugtrio","condition":"Lv. 26","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[0,328],[1,10],[1,28],[1,45],[1,161],[1,310],[1,400],[12,189],[16,523],[20,389],[24,163],[30,201],[36,91],[42,414],[48,89],[54,90]],"machine":[97,34,523,204,174,91,38,414,89,283,203,263,492,416,63,341,189,182,156,179,350,157,317,328,201,815,421,214,188,482,479,446,707,444,164,241,14,36,851,168,675,253],"egg":[],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"me2pt5-239","name":"Team Rocket's Dugtrio","set":"Ascended Heroes","date":"2026-01-30","rarity":"Illustration Rare","number":"239","artist":"Whisker","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me2pt5-239/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me2pt5-239/large"},{"id":"me2pt5-101","name":"Team Rocket's Dugtrio","set":"Ascended Heroes","date":"2026-01-30","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"101","artist":"KEIICHIRO ITO","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me2pt5-101/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me2pt5-101/large"},{"id":"sv8-123","name":"Alolan Dugtrio","set":"Surging Sparks","date":"2024-11-08","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"123","artist":null,"img":"sv8/123"},{"id":"sv8-208","name":"Alolan Dugtrio","set":"Sur